  "details": "It's currently the 31's of July however everything was working fine as of the 30th. On the 29th I got on for a group event a community i'm a part of hosts and everything was fine then. I have not restarted my computer since then, no updates have happened that i'm aware of. I tried getting on to join some friends tonight (the 31st) and my PC immediately hit a BSOD. The original error was \"Kernel Mode Heap Corruption\" and the next and subsequent BSOD's were Kmode Exception Not Handled. I know EAC does stuff in the Kernel. I've clean installed VRC. I've doublechecked everything as according to your troubleshooting page about EAC problems. None of it has worked. I suggest you look into your implementation of EAC and fix it or remove it until your EAC implementation is actually ready for prime time.\nAny troubleshooting steps I haven't already taken would be great to try. I've loaded other VR apps no problem and other games utilizing EAC. It's on your end as far as I can tell. Please fix. Other platforms are looking enticing all a sudden...",
